 "title": "Post Graduate Programme in Enterprise Management | Executive Programs for Working Professional",
 "text": "Post Graduate Programme in Enterprise Management (PGPEM)\nDURATION\nTwo-year weekend\nprogramme\n \nENROLLED IN 2026\n79 students\n \nDownload Brochure\n\nThe Post Graduate Programme in Enterprise Management leading to:\n\nMaster of Business Administration (MBA)\n\n \n\n   \n\nThe PGPEM is a programme designed for working mid-level and senior executives with a minimum of six years of work experience after graduation. Launched in 1998, the programme is rigorous and scheduled on weekends to make it accessible to those who do not want to leave their jobs while pursuing a master’s degree..\n\nThe purpose of the programme is to complement the excellent functional knowledge and experience that participants possess with contemporary management knowledge, thereby preparing them to manage greater responsibilities in a liberalized and globalized economy.\n\nStudents are provided a strong grounding in general management through the core courses in the first year and ample opportunity to acquire specialized knowledge through a rich choice of electives in the second year. A unique feature of this programme is that students can choose not only from the electives offered by the PGPEM but also from the other degree-granting programmes at IIMB.\n\nThe on-campus classes for the PGPEM are offered over the weekends, allowing students the opportunity to pursue a quality management programme without compromising on their fulltime jobs. The PGPEM also provides participants opportunities to go on full-term exchange programmes with IIMB's international partner institutions.\n\nThe graduates of the PGPEM are part of the IIMB Alumni Association. IIMB has a global alumni network with chapters in all major cities in India and several major cities across the world. The alumni organize regular and special events, sometimes in collaboration with the pan-IIM network, to facilitate knowledge sharing and networking.\n\nMessage from the Chairperson\n\nProfessor Ashis Mishra\n\nChairperson, Master of Business Administration (MBA), Two-year Programme for Working Professionals\n\n The Post Graduate Program in Enterprise Management (PGPEM) is a comprehensive and rigorous management program designed for working professionals to enhance their managerial skills and advance their careers without interrupting their work commitments. The PGPEM is a unique programme unlike any other traditional degree granting programme; it is a pathway to personal and professional growth, a platform for honing your leadership skills, and an opportunity to expand your horizons in the ever-evolving landscape of business and management.\n\nPGPEM programs usually span over a period of 2 years (min) to 5 years (max), depending on the flexibility desired by the students. The curriculum of PGPEM programs covers a wide range of management topics such as finance, marketing, operations, human resources, strategy, leadership, and entrepreneurship. The courses are designed to provide participants with a holistic understanding of various business functions and develop their analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making skills. PGPEM program often employs a combination of teaching methods including lectures, case studies, group discussions, projects, simulations, and workshops. This diverse pedagogical approach helps participants apply theoretical concepts to real-world business scenarios and develop practical skills relevant to their roles. \n\nAccreditation and Rankings\n\nStudent Achievements\nView all\n\nPGPEM students advance to top 10 at Harvard Global Case Competition\n\nRead More  >\n\nCampus win for PGPEM team at Hult Prize 2025 at IIM Bangalore\n\nRead More  >\n\nNational win for PGPEM team at IIM Kozhikode’s PowerUp strategy challenge\n\nRead More  >\nPGPEM in the News\nPrajwalan 2026: PGPEM’s annual sports extravaganza concludes in full swing\nPGPEM students celebrate culture and community at Pehel 2026\nPGPEM welcomes 79 students to the batch of 2026–28 on 4 April 2026\nIIM Bangalore’s PGPEM propels into global top 100: FT EMBA Ranking 2025\nInnoventure 2025 bets big on start-ups as the next global growth engine\nConferences\nDrishti 2025\nDrishti 2024\nDrishti 2022\nLeadership & Spirituality\n\nPGPEM at IIMB set to host annual business and cultural summit: Drishti 2025\n\nDeliberating the 'Future in Focus', the annual two-day event will be held on 14 & 15 November 2025\n\nRead more...\n\nLeaderSpeak Series\nTalk on scaling platform business by Ashok Shastry on May 15\n\nCohort 21 of the Post Graduate Programme in Enterprise Management (PGPEM) hosted a talk by Ashok Shastry, CEO & Co-founder, DriveU, as part of their ‘LeaderSpeak’ series. Ashok Shastry is a young entrepreneur, who started DriveU, in May 2015, with the dual objective of “making life simple for millions of car owners across India through technology while creating reliable incomes for those who need it the most”. Ashok talked about his entrepreneurial journey, focusing on scaling platform business.\n\nWatch here\n\nDesign provides beautiful solutions and motivates users to try a product\n\nFounder and Design Director of Lollypop UI/UX Design Studio Anil Reddy shares his thoughts on how Design can enhance businesses in a session titled, ‘Impact of Design in Growing Businesses’, hosted by IIMB’s Post Graduate Programme in Enterprise Management, as part of the LeaderSpeak Series\n\nRead more\n\nThe CEO who talks clean energy\n\nFrom career mapping to climate change, Ashish Bhandari, MD & CEO Thermax Ltd, shares his insights on a range of issues with students of the weekend MBA at IIMB\n\nRead more\n\nTechnology is always an enabler for business and the key is to make the right choices in business\n\nKavitha Siddada, Global IT Head of Design Engineering at Shell, shares her insights on technology leadership and inclusion in Retail IT in a session titled, ‘Technology Leadership – Retail Enterprises’, hosted by IIMB’s Post Graduate Programme in Enterprise Management\n\nRead more\n\nVideos\nView all\n\nTestimonials\nView all\nVideo\nText\n\nRedefining Learning Beyond the Classroom - Siny J Fernandes’ Journey through PGPEM at IIMB\n\nRakesh's Journey at IIMB - Merging Aerospace Expertise with Strategic Leadership through PGPEM\n\nUnsettle to Settle for More: Priya Agarwal on Finding Her Dream Again with PGPEM at IIMB\n\nFrom Experience to Expertise: Dhaval Trivedi on Expanding His Leadership Vision with PGPEM\n\nFAQs\nHow is the PGPEM different from the PGP?\n\nThe PGPEM is focused on mid-career and senior executives. The programme design acknowledges that executives with work experience have different needs and a different appreciation of management education.\n\nThe Post Graduate Programme in Management (PGP) has a focus on professionals at the entry levels. While some participants have work experience, a majority of the participants are freshers. The programme design for the PGP recognizes the lack of work experience among participants and is geared to providing relevant knowledge for entry level positions in a variety of industries.\n\nHow is the PGPEM different from the EPGP?\nHow is the PGPEM different from the EGMP?\nIs there scholarship or bank loan facility for programme?\nDoes programme provide the participant with flexibility to take a break for work-related travel outside the city/country or attend to the other priorities?\nDoes the programme provide the participant with an opportunity to acquire international exposure?\nWhat level and type of work experience I need to have?\nWhat is the minimum CAT / GMAT/ GRE / IIMB Test score required to apply?\nWhat is preferred test for admission into PGPEM?\nWhat i have to do once I am shortlisted for the personal interview?",
